{"kind":"propose","text":"H2 retained bytes for planner and kernel review. Let E be entryBytes, U be usesPerEntry, and P_i the canonical page cap for declared read i. Derive preflight charges member prepare plus the larger of commit and abandon, at most 2E if each canonical entry obeys E. The order scope separately charges allocation plus the largest resolution, hole or expiry entry and its retained inputs. Each retained foreign entry and its possible birth cost at most 2E under the receiver’s entry allowance. Charge ordinary facts through current fieldRetainedBytes, then add 2E for each additional distinct member ordering fact needed by the larger prepare-plus-terminal branch. The combined per-entry uses must fit U. The local prepare reference adds no birth, and the member does not pay for the order scope’s journal a second time. Charge sum(P_i) for the four or fewer declared group pages. Keep pages in their own domain. Reuse the selected branch’s existing detached text, typed value, observation and rule-input terms. The text cap is 6 × min(field max, textBytes) + 2, and distinct rule inputs cost up to ruleInputBytes each. The post-judgment quote uses the actual checked draft and retained inputs. Credit an existing retained key only after matching domain, digest and size against the same retained state. Add independent duties and take the per-dimension maximum for terminal alternatives. H4 owns durable transfer or release. The contract already names the six input variants, but bytes/src/records.ts rejects their wire rows and the retained page. Before adding their byte formulas to source, please rule on a canonical page ceiling (AT_PAGE_ITEMS alone bounds only rows), exact allocation, order-head, cut and terminal proof inventory within uses, and whether pending/fence/cut bookkeeping counts toward logical scopeBytes. The current SQLite byte calculation covers journal/retained domains and accepted keys. The current AtRead success type has a non-null entry; §5.5's null left case is outside v1 and can stay with later work. For the current H2 delivery refusal, I can preserve bounded creation acceptance by giving the derive source-check result an explicit source-not-effective reason under its existing discriminator, until H4 exposes the runtime result. Expanding the existing shared DeliveryRefusal union alone would widen the creation answer. Please flag if the H2 kernel cut should instead split those public contract types now."}